{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 37, :comments ["<b>A rod of poplar.</b> A rod of לבנה, and it is cedar from the trees of Lebanon — that is, a moist rod of לבנה." "<b>And hazel and chestnut.</b> Its meaning is: a rod from a tree whose name is לוז, and it is almonds, and from the chestnut tree." "<b>And he peeled in them white streaks.</b> Its meaning is: he peeled away from those rods part of the bark, which is black, and where he peeled it appeared white, and where the bark remained upon it, it was black. This is מחשוף הלבן — 'the exposed white' is the white that is upon the rods. And these rods which he peeled, he set them in the troughs, in the water channels. When he wanted speckled ones, he would peel places on the rods, after the manner of נקודות הכסף ('silver drops'); thus they were speckled — the place of the removal of the bark was white and the place of the bark was black, and then speckled ones were born. And when he wanted streaked ones, he would peel part of the rods at the top and leave the peeled part on part of the rods at the bottom. And when he wanted dark among the sheep, he would not peel at all, but the hue, which is black, remained upon it, and then dark ones were born. And when he wanted brindled ones, he would not peel at all, for that hue was smoky-black. And Jacob had many rods of species of cedar in this hue." "<b>And it came to pass —</b> this matter was for Jacob a thing of wisdom, and the secret of nature was mingled with miracle. For there was a natural aspect on the side of the peeling of the rods, and on the other side it was a pure miracle, that they were not born according to the mothers — if black, black; if white, white. And if you should say that the image of the rods before the eyes of the flock overcame simple nature, none the less — that they should all be in the hue of the rods, which is the image, and not even one in the hue of the mothers, is impossible without a miracle. And so Jacob said: ״ואלהי אבי היה עמדי״ (Genesis 31:5). This comes to teach that without the miracle and the help of Elohim, the matter would not have been accomplished by the peeling of the rods alone. And so he said further: ״ויצל אלהים את מקנה אביכם ויתן לי״ (Genesis 31:9). He attributed the matter to Elohim, who did wondrously with him."], :book :genesis, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 30, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:16:40.741974808Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}